Laravel's CSRF protection will block POST requests to the event endpoint by default [1]. In your `bootstrap/app.php` file, add the event route to the CSRF exceptions [1]:

```php title="bootstrap/app.php"
->withMiddleware(function (Middleware $middleware) {
    $middleware->validateCsrfTokens(except: [
        'api/event', // Add this line
    ]);
})
```

Additionally, the Events API returns 202 Accepted even when an event is dropped, usually because `X-Forwarded-For` carries a server IP instead of the visitor's [2]. Inspect the response headers for `x-plausible-dropped: 1`, which indicates the event was rejected by bot filtering [3].

